steps.detail:
Use the matching protocol by its title:
- chest pain: Chest pain or heart attack protocol;
- face drooping, arm drifting, slurred speech: Stroke protocol;
- wheezing in someone with asthma: Asthma attack protocol;
- swelling of the face, lips or tongue, hives, or a throat closing: Anaphylaxis (severe allergic reaction) protocol.

AHA 2024 (Class 3: Harm): physical counterpressure manoeuvres are not recommended when signs of a heart attack or stroke come with the faint feeling.

Call 911 if you have signal. If not, send someone for help and prepare to move the casualty.
